# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Shell scripts MUST stay LF. core.autocrlf=true would otherwise hand a fresh
# Windows clone CRLF .sh files, and bash inside WSL fails on the carriage return
# with "$'\r': command not found" — setup-console-wsl.sh dies on line 1. The
# repo happened to hold LF working copies, so this never surfaced locally.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Batch files MUST stay CRLF, for the same reason in reverse. CMD parses labels by
# line, and an LF-only .bat fails with "The system cannot find the batch label
# specified" - `goto :summary` in run-all.bat dies and every `call` misfires. A clone
# with core.autocrlf=false (or any editor writing LF) would produce exactly that.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
